Yes—separate GitHub repo + separate Supabase project is the structurally correct move for “Naruto”.

This prevents coupling with JARVIS, avoids schema contamination, and makes the swarm OS independently evolvable.


---

RESPONSE

1. Recommended Isolation Strategy

Hard separation principle

Naruto should be treated as a standalone distributed system, not a module inside JARVIS.

System	Responsibility

JARVIS	governance + memory + orchestration brain
Naruto	swarm execution OS
Supabase (Naruto)	isolated mission + clone state
GitHub (Naruto)	execution runtime + MCP server


This avoids:

schema collisions

memory interference

accidental coupling of governance rules

version drift between systems



---

2. Why separation matters (core systems reasoning)

A. State contamination risk

If shared Supabase:

clone data leaks into JARVIS memory graphs

event logs become ambiguous (who owns truth?)


B. Execution boundary clarity

Naruto is:

> high-concurrency execution layer



JARVIS is:

> deterministic control + reasoning layer



Mixing them breaks traceability.


