4. Separate Supabase Project Design

Project name:

naruto-swarm-db

Tables:

naruto_missions

naruto_clones

naruto_events (critical addition)

naruto_memory_global


This keeps it:

versioned

disposable

experiment-safe



---

5. Event Log Layer (strongly recommended)

This is what makes the system real OS-like.

create table naruto_events (
  event_id serial primary key,
  mission_id text,
  clone_id int,
  event_type text,
  payload jsonb,
  timestamp timestamp default now()
);

This enables:

full replay

debugging swarm decisions

audit trails for every clone action



---

6. Integration Model (JARVIS ↔ Naruto)

Interaction rule

JARVIS never runs clones directly.

Instead:

JARVIS
  ↓ (mission spec)
Naruto Controller (MCP)
  ↓
Supabase + Workers
  ↓
Aggregated output
  ↓
JARVIS (evaluation only)

This enforces:

separation of reasoning vs execution

clean scaling boundary

no recursive self-interference



---

7. Minimal MVP Scope (important constraint)

Start with only:

spawn clone

assign task

execute LLM call

store output

aggregate results


Do NOT add yet:

recursive spawning

autonomous role evolution

multi-layer memory compression


Those come later.


